    "text": "4 hours ago DETROIT – A.B. Ford Park on Detroit’s east side is getting a new lease on life after a multi-million dollar facelift. The park had sat empty since 2020, but thanks to funding from the American Rescue Plan Act and the city’s Strategic Neighborhood Fund, the city transformed the space into a new waterfront gathering spot. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 3",
